WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.083
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.383 --> 00:00:08.828
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.128 --> 00:00:13.916
Unit thirteen: Wish & If Only. Today you will express regrets and wishes.

4
00:00:14.216 --> 00:00:17.031
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.967 --> 00:00:21.234
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.083 --> 00:00:23.166
I wish.

7
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.974
I wish means a way to express an unreal wish.

8
00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:29.095
I wish I were taller.

9
00:00:29.683 --> 00:00:32.045
Your turn. Say: I wish.

10
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:35.797
I wish.

11
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.574
If only.

12
00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:40.467
If only means a stronger wish.

13
00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:42.526
If only I knew.

14
00:00:43.117 --> 00:00:45.432
Your turn. Say: If only.

15
00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:49.326
If only.

16
00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:50.945
Regret.

17
00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:54.263
Regret means sadness about the past.

18
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.211
I regret nothing.

19
00:00:56.817 --> 00:00:59.365
Your turn. Say: Regret.

20
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.085
Regret.

21
00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:05.118
Unreal present.

22
00:01:06.117 --> 00:01:10.090
Unreal present means a present situation that is not true.

23
00:01:10.683 --> 00:01:12.172
An unreal present.

24
00:01:12.783 --> 00:01:15.819
Your turn. Say: Unreal present.

25
00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.179
Unreal present.

26
00:01:20.917 --> 00:01:22.254
Unreal past.

27
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.666
Unreal past means a past situation that did not happen.

28
00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.890
An unreal past.

29
00:01:29.483 --> 00:01:32.542
Your turn. Say: Unreal past.

30
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.703
Unreal past.

31
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.124
Wish + past simple.

32
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:42.824
Wish + past simple means a present wish.

33
00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:45.045
I wish I had a car.

34
00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:49.045
Your turn. Say: Wish + past simple.

35
00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.853
Wish + past simple.

36
00:01:54.617 --> 00:01:56.256
Wish + past perfect.

37
00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.097
Wish + past perfect means a past regret.

38
00:02:00.683 --> 00:02:02.102
I wish I had studied.

39
00:02:02.717 --> 00:02:06.449
Your turn. Say: Wish + past perfect.

40
00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.183
Wish + past perfect.

41
00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:12.777
Longing.

42
00:02:13.783 --> 00:02:15.864
Longing means a strong wish.

43
00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:17.823
A longing for home.

44
00:02:18.417 --> 00:02:21.382
Your turn. Say: Longing.

45
00:02:24.233 --> 00:02:25.374
Longing.

46
00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:29.887
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.539
Visal, what do you wish were different in your life?

48
00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:44.675
I wish I had more free time. After wish we use the past simple for a present situation that we want to change: I wish I lived near the sea.

49
00:02:45.783 --> 00:02:47.075
And for the past?

50
00:02:48.183 --> 00:02:59.372
We use the past perfect: I wish I had studied harder. If only is stronger: If only I had listened. Both show regret and longing about the unreal past.

51
00:03:00.483 --> 00:03:01.728
What about would?

52
00:03:02.817 --> 00:03:13.378
I wish you would stop shouting expresses annoyance about someone's behaviour. We cannot use I wish I would. Use were for all persons: I wish he were here.

53
00:03:14.533 --> 00:03:16.196
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:21.604
Grammar focus: Wish and if only: past simple, past perfect, would.

55
00:03:21.904 --> 00:03:23.183
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:23.883 --> 00:03:25.836
I wish I had more free time.

57
00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.657
If only I had listened to her.

58
00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.433
I wish you would stop shouting.

59
00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:41.582
Wish + past simple = present wish. Wish + past perfect = past regret. Wish + would = annoyance. Use were for all persons.

60
00:03:42.317 --> 00:03:45.700
Be careful! Don't say: I wish I will have time.

61
00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:49.689
Say: I wish I had time.

62
00:03:49.989 --> 00:03:51.734
Use the past after wish.

63
00:03:52.533 --> 00:03:54.965
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:56.803
If Only….

65
00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.265
I wish I had more free time to read.

66
00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:02.905
If only I had listened to my mother's advice.

67
00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.863
I wish I lived near the sea, but it is far away.

68
00:04:07.867 --> 00:04:10.772
I wish my neighbours would stop playing loud music.

69
00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:13.778
There is a longing in every wish.

70
00:04:14.867 --> 00:04:18.729
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:19.583 --> 00:04:22.120
I wish I blank a car. (present)

72
00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:25.852
A, have. B, had. C, would have.

73
00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.481
The answer is B: had.

74
00:04:32.617 --> 00:04:35.141
I wish I blank harder. (past)

75
00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:39.304
A, studied. B, had studied. C, would study.

76
00:04:42.867 --> 00:04:44.936
The answer is B: had studied.

77
00:04:46.083 --> 00:04:47.816
I wish you blank stop shouting.

78
00:04:48.116 --> 00:04:50.980
A, would. B, had. C, were.

79
00:04:54.533 --> 00:04:56.603
The answer is A: would.

80
00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.123
Which is correct?

81
00:04:59.423 --> 00:05:04.643
A, I wish I was rich.. B, I wish I were rich.. C, I wish I will be rich..

82
00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.652
The answer is B: I wish I were rich..

83
00:05:11.817 --> 00:05:14.757
According to the reading, what do the neighbours play?

84
00:05:15.057 --> 00:05:18.803
A, loud music. B, the guitar. C, the radio.

85
00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:24.471
The answer is A: loud music.

86
00:05:25.667 --> 00:05:28.888
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:32.609
Write a sentence expressing a wish about your own life.

88
00:05:41.417 --> 00:05:42.963
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:43.263 --> 00:05:56.881
I wish I had more time to travel. If only I had learned a musical instrument when I was young. I wish my neighbours would be quieter. Each sentence uses a different form after wish.

90
00:05:57.181 --> 00:05:59.006
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:59.917 --> 00:06:06.586
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and wish and if only: past simple, past perfect, would.

92
00:06:06.886 --> 00:06:10.874
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

93
00:06:11.174 --> 00:06:13.919
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:14.219 --> 00:06:16.871
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

